          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em semisimple category
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            in which each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finitely many
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simple+objects"} simple objects
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semisimple+abelian+category"}> semisimple abelian category
                )
              %br/
              An
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
              is called
              %strong semisimple
              if every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semisimple+object"} semisimple object
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finitely many
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simple+objects"} simple objects
          %p
            Alternatively, at least over an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraically+closed+field"} algebraically closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          %p
          #SemisimpleLinearCategory.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              %strong (semisimple linear category)
              %br/
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+category"} linear category
              (that is, a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched over
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
              = succeed ")" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+category"} tensor category
              %strong semisimple
              if:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  it has
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+product"} finite
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/biproducts"} biproducts
                %p
                  (usually called ‘
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sums"}> direct sums
                  ’),
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+idempotent"} idempotents split
                %p
                  (so we say that it ‘has
                  = succeed "\u2019" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobjects"} subobjects
                  = succeed "\u2019)," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retracts"} retracts
              %li
                %p
                  there exist
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_i
                  labeled by an index
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
                  such that
                %ol
                  %li
                    %p
                      for any
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ,
                            %mi j
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i, j
                      of indices we have an
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                    #eq:SimplicityIsomorphism.maruku-equation
                      %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi Hom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi i
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mo ≅
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %msub
                              %mi δ
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mi j
                            %mi k
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo ,
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                            Hom(X_i, X_j)
                            \\;\cong\;
                            \\delta_{i j} k
                            \\,,
                    %p
                      where
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi δ
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
                      denotes the
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kronecker+delta"} Kronecker delta
                      and
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi k
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                      the
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
                    %p
                      (such objects are called
                      = succeed ")," do
                        %em
                          %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simple+object"} simple
                  %li
                    %p
                      for any
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
                      of
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                      = succeed "," do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi V
                              %mo ,
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mi W
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V,\,W
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
                      map
                    #eq:CompositionIsomorphism.maruku-equation
                      %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi I
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mi Hom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi V
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mi Hom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi i
                            %mo ,
                            %mi W
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mi Hom
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi V
                            %mo ,
                            %mi W
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                            \\bigoplus_{i \in I}
                            \\,
                            Hom(V, X_i)
                            \\,\otimes\,
                            Hom(X_i, W)
                            \\longrightarrow
                            Hom(V, W)
                    %p
                      is an
                      = succeed "." do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                %p
                  (If the field
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                  is not
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraically+closed+field"} algebraically closed
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simple+object"} simple object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  can have a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite-dimensional+vector+space"} finite-dimensional
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/division+algebra"} division algebra
                  other than
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                  itself as its
                  = succeed ".)" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphism+algebra"} endomorphism algebra
            %p
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Müger03"} Müger (2003, p. 6)
          %p
          #DirectSumDecompositionintoSimples.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (direct sum decomposition into simple objects)
              %br/
              Definition
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SemisimpleLinearCategory"}
              implies that every object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simple+objects"} simple objects
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_i
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              The third item of the definition is equivalent to stipulating that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(X_i, V)
              is in canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+vector+space"} duality
              with the vector space
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(V, X_i)
            %ol
              %li
                %p a pairing
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:columnalign => "center center center", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi Hom
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi V
                              %mo ,
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mi i
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo ⊗
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mi Hom
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mi i
                              %mo ,
                              %mi V
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mo ⟶
                            %mtd
                              %mi Hom
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mi i
                              %mo ,
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mi i
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mo ≃
                            %mtd
                              %mi k
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi f
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo ⊗
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mi g
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↦
                            %mtd
                              %mi f
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo ∘
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mi g
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                  %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\begin{array}{ccc}
                        Hom(V, X_i)
                        \\,\otimes\,
                        Hom(X_i, V)
                        \&amp;
                        \\longrightarrow
                        \&amp;
                        Hom(X_i, X_i)
                        \&amp;\simeq&amp;
                        k
                        \\\
                        f \,\otimes\, g
                        \&amp;\mapsto&amp;
                        f \,\circ\, g
                        \\mathrlap{\,,}
                        \\end{array}
                %p
                  where on the right we used
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SimplicityIsomorphism"} (1)
              %li
                %p a copairing
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ⋅
                        %msub
                          %mi Id
                          %mi B
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ↪
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi Hom
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi V
                        %mo ,
                        %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi Hom
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi Hom
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi V
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                          %mrow
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        k \cdot Id_B
                        \\;\hookrightarrow\;
                        Hom(V,V)
                        \\longrightarrow
                        Hom(X_i, V)
                        \\otimes
                        Hom(V, X_i)
                        \\mathrlap{\,,}
                %p
                  where on the right we used
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:CompositionIsomorphism"} (2)
            %p
              and one checks that these satisfy the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangle+identities"} triangle identities
              and as such exhibit
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+vector+spaces"} dual vector spaces
            %p
              Hence if we choose a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+basis"} linear basis
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi p
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\big\{
                    a_{i,p}
                    \\,\colon\,
                    X_i
                    \\rightarrow V
                    \\big\}
            %p
              for each
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(X_i, V)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} {
                    %msubsup
                      %mi a
                      %mi i
                      %mi p
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi V
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\big\{
                    a_i^p
                    \\,\colon\,
                    V \rightarrow X_i
                    \\big\}
            %p satisfying
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi a
                      %mi i
                      %mi p
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mi j
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                    %msubsup
                      %mi δ
                      %mi p
                      %mi q
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mtext and
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi p
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi p
                    %msubsup
                      %mi a
                      %mi i
                      %mi p
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} id
                      %mi V
                    %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    a_i^p a_{j,q}
                    \\;=\;
                    \\delta_{i j} \delta_p^q
                    \\;\;\; \text{and} \;\;\;
                    \\sum_{i,p} a_{i,p} a_i^p
                    \\;=\; \id_V
                    \\mathrlap{\,.}
            %p
              This says precisely that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              has been expressed as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              of the
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_i
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SemisimpleLinearCategory"}
              (of semisimple linear categories) does not use the concept of
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/biproduct"} biproduct
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retract"} retract
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              For a category to be semisimple, it needs to have a certain directional symmetry in its hom-sets, namely that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(V, W)
              must at least have the same dimension as
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi W
                      %mo ,
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(W,V)
              %em fail
              to be semisimple. For instance, the category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Rep
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rep(A)
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representations"} representations
              of an algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              will rarely be semisimple, precisely because there is no relation between
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(V, W)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi W
                    %mo ,
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(W,V)
              in general. Again, this can be traced back to the original algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              not having any ‘symmetry’ like the inverse operation in a group.
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              As far as ‘duality’ on the hom-sets is concerned, one might have a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \colon C \rightarrow C
              from the category to itself with the property that there are canonical isomorphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi W
                    %mo ,
                    %mi S
                    %mi V
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∨
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom(V, W) \cong Hom(W, S V)^\vee
            %p
              where “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∨
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vee
              ” denotes the ordinary linear dual of a vector space. Such a functor is called a
              %em Serre functor
              in algebraic geometry, and indeed there is precisely such a functor on the derived category of coherent sheaves on a complex manifold — it is given by tensoring with the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+line+bundle"} canonical line bundle
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-Hilbert+space"} 2-Hilbert spaces
              = succeed "-operation" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo :
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ,
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi W
                      %mo ,
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} * : Hom(V, W) \rightarrow Hom(W,V)
              = succeed "-algebra," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The archetypical simple example is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinDimVect"} FinDimVect
                itself, the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+dimensional+vector+spaces"} finite dimensional vector spaces
                over some
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
                class of simple objects: given by
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                itself.
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+representations"} category of finite-dimensional complex representations
                of a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+group"} compact Lie group
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                is semisimple, with the simple objects being precisely the
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+representation"} irreducible representation
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schur%27s+lemma"} Schur's lemma
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                is not a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+group"} compact Lie group
                = succeed "\u2019." do
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    direct integral
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/direct+integral"} ?
            %li
              %p
                Every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fusion+category"} fusion category
                is a semisimple category.
          %h2#references References
          %p Various alternative definitions of semisimple category appear in the literature, and a number are compared here:
          %ul
            %li
              James Bailie, Semisimple categories (
              %a{:href => "https://jameshbailie.github.io/Papers/papers/Semisimple.pdf"}> pdf
              \.
          %p For example, he compares a definition of “abelian semisimple category”(an abelian category where every object is a direct sum of a possibly infinite number of simple objects) with “Müger semisimple” categories as discussed here:
          %ul
            %li{:id => "Müger03"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+M%C3%BCger"}> Michael Müger
              , p. 6 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em From Subfactors to Categories and Topology I. Frobenius algebras in and Morita equivalence classes of tensor categories
              %strong 180
              (2003) 81-157 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0111204"}> arXiv:math/0111204
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0022-4049(02)00247-5"} doi:10.1016/S0022-4049(02)00247-5
          %p
            There is a
            %a{:href => "http://nforum.ncatlab.org/discussion/1120/semisimple-category/?Focus=42783#Comment_42783"} related discussion on the nForum
            and a
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/questions/442953/what-is-the-correct-definition-of-semisimple-linear-category"} discussion on MathOverflow
        .revisedby
